Q. How do you handle StaleElementReferenceException?
Ans:  StaleElementReferenceException occurs when a WebElement reference becomes stale 
  (DOM has been refreshed). 
  Solutions: 
  1. Re-locate the element after action: 
    WebElement element = driver.findElement(By.id("dynamicElement")); 
  element.click(); 
  // DOM refreshes 
  element = driver.findElement(By.id("dynamicElement")); // Re-locate 
  element.sendKeys("text"); 
  2. Use Explicit Wait with WebDriverWait: 
    WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10)); 
  WebElement element = 
  wait.until(ExpectedConditions.presenceOfElementLocated(By.id("element")
  )); 
  element.click(); 
  3. Wrap in Try-Catch and Retry: 
    int attempts = 0; 
  while (attempts < 3) { 
      try { 
          driver.findElement(By.id("element")).click(); 
          break; 
      } catch (StaleElementReferenceException e) { 
          attempts++; 
      } 
  } 

